deploy/gvisor/README.md:102:| `BLASTBOX_GVISOR_WARM_ARGV` | `["python3","/opt/blastbox/run_warm.py"]` | JSON list; argv of the warm entrypoint (see below). Must be a non-empty list of strings or it falls back to the default. **venv-based engine images** (e.g. clippyshot installs into `/opt/clippyshot`) must point this at the venv interpreter — `["/opt/clippyshot/bin/python3", …]` — because the default bare `python3` resolves on the spec `PATH` to the *system* interpreter, which can't `import blastbox`/the engine package (silent `ModuleNotFoundError` → never reaches READY → ready-timeout) |
deploy/gvisor/README.md:103:| `BLASTBOX_GVISOR_LD_PRELOAD` | _(unset)_ | Set to `/opt/clippyshot/accept-retry.so` for the soffice warm container |
deploy/gvisor/README.md:104:| `BLASTBOX_GVISOR_EXTRA_ENV` | `[]` | JSON array of `"KEY=VALUE"` strings appended to the worker's OCI `process.env`. Engine-agnostic passthrough for env the image can't bake (the OCI spec is built from scratch; image `ENV` is dropped). Malformed input is ignored, not fatal. ClippyShot needs `CLIPPYSHOT_SANDBOX=container` + `CLIPPYSHOT_WARN_ON_INSECURE=1` here (see recipe below) |
deploy/gvisor/README.md:105:| `BLASTBOX_GVISOR_PLATFORM` | _(runsc default)_ | `ptrace` or `kvm`; leave unset to let runsc choose |
deploy/gvisor/README.md:106:| `BLASTBOX_GVISOR_CPUFEATURES` | _(unset)_ | `dev.gvisor.internal.cpufeatures` OCI annotation for cross-host CPU pinning |
deploy/gvisor/README.md:107:| `BLASTBOX_SNAPSHOT_SETTLE_S` | `1.0` | Seconds to wait after restore before sending the job (post-restore settle) |
deploy/gvisor/README.md:108:| `BLASTBOX_GVISOR_NPROC` | `4096` | `RLIMIT_NPROC` for the warm worker tree (fork-bomb bound) |
deploy/gvisor/README.md:109:| `BLASTBOX_GVISOR_NOFILE` | `65536` | `RLIMIT_NOFILE` for the warm worker tree (fd-exhaustion bound) |
