     1	"""URL-grabber engine — the REFERENCE EXAMPLE for the network overlay.
     2	
     3	blastbox ships no domain engines (those live in their own repos); this is one of two runnable
     4	*examples* (with ``detonate``), here to demonstrate the opt-in egress overlay end-to-end. Given an
     5	input file containing a single URL, it does ONE bounded HTTP GET and seals the response body as an
     6	artifact plus structured metadata (status, final URL after redirects, content-type, server,
     7	body sha256/len). It does NOT execute or render anything — it is a *fetch*, not a browser.
     8	
     9	As the first *network* consumer of the netpolicy/egress tiers it shows the safe-egress story: under
    10	``net_policy=fakenet`` it exercises the whole pipe against a sinkhole; under ``net_policy=tor`` it
    11	fetches attribution-protected. Both example tiers need no credentials.
    12	
    13	Isolation + egress are the dispatcher's job: this engine runs in a disposable hardened worker
    14	whose network is whatever the resolved netpolicy granted —
    15	  * ``net_policy=fakenet`` → FakeNet-NG answers (safe smoke test of the whole stack),
    16	  * ``net_policy=socks``/``vpn`` → real fetch through tor / PIA (attribution-protected),
    17	  * ``net_policy=none`` → the fetch simply fails closed (recorded, not an error).
    18	netd captures the worker's pcap independently and the host seals it alongside this engine's body.
    19	
    20	A failed reach-out (DNS NXDOMAIN, connection refused, timeout) is a NORMAL result for a dead /
    21	sinkholed malware URL → ``status="ok"`` with the error recorded, NOT ``engine_error`` (which would
    22	fail the job). Only a malformed input URL is ``rejected``.
    23	
    24	SSRF note: this engine does NOT screen the target host (it will GET ``http://169.254.169.254/…``,
    25	``http://127.0.0.1``, RFC1918, etc.). That is deliberate — SSRF containment is delegated ENTIRELY to
    26	the netpolicy/egress isolation: the worker is network-confined to the resolved exit (none/fakenet/
    27	proxy/vpn) and cannot reach a host metadata endpoint or internal service. The corollary: urlgrab must
    28	never be paired with a ``direct`` personality on a bridge that can reach internal/host services.
    29	
    30	The actual fetch is an injected seam (``fetch_fn``) so the engine logic is unit-testable without a
