{"candidate_id":"BB-FD-S0014-001","title":"Libvirt VM egress policy can apply without fail-closed MAC and IPv6 guards","affected_locations":[{"label":"entrypoint/wrapper","path":"src/blastbox/host/runtime/libvirt_vm.py","line":217},{"label":"entrypoint/wrapper","path":"src/blastbox/host/runtime/libvirt_vm.py","line":239},{"label":"root_control","path":"src/blastbox/host/runtime/libvirt_egress.py","line":320},{"label":"broken_control","path":"src/blastbox/host/runtime/libvirt_egress.py","line":324},{"label":"broken_control","path":"src/blastbox/host/runtime/libvirt_egress.py","line":335},{"label":"sink","path":"src/blastbox/host/runtime/libvirt_egress.py","line":338}],"instance_key":"egress-bypass:src/blastbox/host/runtime/libvirt_egress.py:324","attacker_controlled_source":"A malicious document or exploited in-guest agent/tool running inside a libvirt VM worker can control guest network behavior after the VM is handed work, including changing its source IPv4 address if it has guest admin/root or using IPv6 traffic if the libvirt network provides IPv6. The worker IP and MAC are host-discovered, but slot.mac can be None.","broken_control_or_sink":"LibvirtEgress.apply installs the VM egress policy as an IPv4 FORWARD jump scoped to -s <worker_ip>. The anti-spoof rule that would drop packets from the worker MAC with a different source IP is installed only if mac is truthy, and the IPv6 drop rule is also conditional on mac and is invoked without check=True, so ip6tables failure does not abort or roll back policy application.","impact":"A compromised VM worker can bypass intended none/drop, tor, VPN, egress_ports, or block_internal controls by changing its source IPv4 address when the MAC guard is absent, or by sending IPv6 traffic on a v6-capable libvirt network when the unchecked ip6tables guard fails. That can grant direct host-network egress, internal/lateral reachability, metadata-service access, or deanonymize traffic that operators expected to force through a sink/tunnel.","why_plausible":"The code comments identify the exact re-IP bypass risk and install a MAC anti-spoof rule to address it, but the rule is optional. libvirt_vm.py assigns slot.mac from _domain_mac(), whose return type is str | None, and calls LibvirtEgress.apply(..., mac=slot.mac) without rejecting None. In libvirt_egress.py apply() then succeeds with only the source-IP jump if mac is absent. The IPv6 guard is described as fail-closed defense but is also guarded by if mac and the _priv(ip6tables ...) return code is ignored. Nearby netd tests for container workers explicitly fail closed when ip6tables fails and IPv6 is reachable, showing the intended boundary that is missing in this VM path.","closest_control":"The closest controls are the source-IP FORWARD jump at libvirt_egress.py:320, the MAC anti-spoof rule at libvirt_egress.py:324-326, and the IPv6 drop at libvirt_egress.py:335-338. They are incomplete because policy installation does not require a MAC for constrained VM exits and does not verify IPv6 is either blocked or absent before marking apply() successful.","validation_evidence_or_gap":"Static validation only in this read-only shard. Evidence establishes an apply-success path with mac=None and an unchecked ip6tables guard. Dynamic validation should exercise a libvirt VM whose MAC discovery fails or is withheld, then confirm a guest re-IP bypasses the -s <worker_ip> chain; separately, on an IPv6-enabled libvirt network, force ip6tables failure and confirm apply() still returns while IPv6 egress remains possible. Counterevidence that may suppress the finding for a deployment: domain MAC discovery is guaranteed and enforced by the caller, and the libvirt worker network is provably IPv4-only with no IPv6 route.","attack_path_facts":["LibvirtVmRuntime.spawn records slot.mac = self._domain_mac(name), but _domain_mac returns None when domiflist parsing finds no MAC.","LibvirtVmRuntime.is_ready applies the configured VmEgressPolicy with mac=slot.mac and does not fail closed when slot.mac is None.","LibvirtEgress.apply creates a per-worker chain and inserts FORWARD -s <worker_ip> -j <chain>, so packets with a different source IP do not enter the worker policy chain.","The anti-spoof rule that would bind the VM MAC to the assigned source IP is conditional on mac; with mac=None there is no rule dropping packets from the same guest NIC using a different source IP.","The IPv6 drop rule is also conditional on mac and its ip6tables return code is ignored, so an IPv6-capable VM network can remain outside the IPv4 iptables policy even when policy application reports success."],"disposition":"candidate","cwe_ids":["CWE-284","CWE-693"]}

