     1	"""Host-side egress policy for libvirt VM workers (the rooter model).
     2	
     3	A container worker is leak-guarded *inside its own netns* (``netwire.leak_guard_rules`` on the
     4	netns OUTPUT chain). A full VM has no netns to ``nsenter`` — its traffic is **forwarded** by the
     5	host, so the same netpolicy personality (exit driver, ``egress_ports``, ``block_internal``) is
     6	enforced on the **host FORWARD chain**, matched on the worker's source IP, in a dedicated
     7	per-worker chain. This is the model the CAPE rooter uses and that win-validator P0 proved
     8	(web-only 53/80/443 + block-internal, real CRL fetched, non-web + RFC1918 blocked).
     9	
    10	Reuses :data:`blastbox.host.netwire._INTERNAL_NETS` and ``parse_egress_ports`` so the VM path and
    11	the container path share one definition of "internal" and one port parser. The exit *routing*
    12	(direct NAT vs vpn/tor policy-route) is host/gateway-specific and layered separately; this module
    13	owns the **filter** (what the worker may reach) — the security-critical half — plus the drop/none
    14	dispositions. A dedicated chain + a single ``-s <ip>`` jump means install/teardown never touches
    15	sibling workers or a co-resident rooter's rules.
    16	"""
