   113	    its exit driver — the rooter half, separate from the FORWARD *filter*. ``direct``/``none``/
   114	    ``drop`` need none (direct = main-table default; none/drop are filter-dropped). Each command is
   115	    idempotently torn down by :meth:`LibvirtEgress.remove` (delete-by-match, no priority guessing).
   116	
   117	    ``egress_ports`` (the policy's destination-port allow-list) port-scopes a tor exit's TCP REDIRECT
   118	    so the allow-list composes with tor; unset means all TCP via tor."""
