# Validation Report: BB-FD-S0016-001

## Finding Title

Unbounded engine metric labels allow API memory and metrics-response DoS when the engine allowlist is open.

## Candidate Metadata

- Candidate id: `BB-FD-S0016-001`
- Instance key: `resource-exhaustion:src/blastbox/observability/metrics.py:32`
- Ledger row id: not provided
- Disposition: `reportable`
- Survives validation: `yes`
- Confidence: `0.78`
- Validation method: static source/control/sink trace plus bounded Prometheus sink-retention proof. Full TestClient HTTP proof was not available because `httpx` is not installed; an in-process async route-endpoint harness hung in this sandbox after app construction, so it was stopped and preserved as an inconclusive artifact.

## Rubric

- [x] Attacker-selected source reaches the affected path from a product boundary: `POST /v1/jobs` accepts the multipart `engine` form field from an API client at `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:473-476`.
- [x] Closest control is incomplete in default/open-allowlist configuration: empty `allowed_engines` accepts any engine unless `BLASTBOX_REQUIRE_ENGINE_ALLOWLIST` is set, at `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:253-272`.
- [x] The sink uses the attacker-selected value as a Prometheus label without canonicalization, length bounding, cardinality bounding, or eviction: `record_job_submitted()` calls `JOBS_SUBMITTED_TOTAL.labels(engine=engine).inc()` at `src/blastbox/observability/metrics.py:30-32`.
- [x] A bounded local proof shows cumulative Prometheus series are retained and serialized on scrape without high memory use.
- [x] Countercontrols and deployment preconditions were checked: nonempty allowlists, `BLASTBOX_REQUIRE_ENGINE_ALLOWLIST`, auth defaults, `/metrics` auth behavior, body/concurrency limits, and later dispatcher rejection.

## Affected Locations From Discovery

- `attacker_controlled_source`: `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:476`
- `root_control`: `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:253`
- `sink_call`: `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:604`
- `sink`: `src/blastbox/observability/metrics.py:32`
- `exposure`: `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:467`

## Source, Control, Sink

Source: a remote API client controls the `engine` form field on `POST /v1/jobs` (`src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:473-476`). The route creates `Job.new(engine=engine, ...)` at `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:526`; `Job.new()` stores that string directly at `src/blastbox/host/jobs/base.py:72-79`.

Closest control: `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:490-498` rejects unknown engines only when `_allowed_engines` is nonempty. The default path reads `BLASTBOX_ALLOWED_ENGINES` and treats an empty set as accept-any at `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:247-253`. `BLASTBOX_REQUIRE_ENGINE_ALLOWLIST` can make that a startup error at `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:259-266`, but it is not default-on. Documentation also lists `BLASTBOX_ALLOWED_ENGINES` default as `""` (all), `BLASTBOX_REQUIRE_ENGINE_ALLOWLIST` default as `0`, `BLASTBOX_API_KEY` default as open, and `BLASTBOX_METRICS_PUBLIC` default as true in `docs/CONFIGURATION.md:25-32`.

Sink: after spooling and store creation, the route calls `record_job_submitted(engine, nbytes)` at `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:604`. `record_job_submitted()` passes `engine` directly into `JOBS_SUBMITTED_TOTAL.labels(engine=engine).inc()` at `src/blastbox/observability/metrics.py:30-32`. `/metrics` returns `generate_latest()` at `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:465-467`, serializing all retained series.

Dispatcher timing: dispatcher rejection of unknown engines is later. The warm and cold dispatch paths look up `self._engines.get(job.engine)` and fail jobs with `"unknown engine"` at `src/blastbox/host/dispatch.py:725-728` and `src/blastbox/host/dispatch.py:965-968`. That later rejection does not undo the already-created submission metric child, and no source reference showed `JOBS_SUBMITTED_TOTAL.remove(...)`, label normalization, or label eviction.

## Preconditions

- Ingress runs with an empty or unset engine allowlist, which is documented as accept-any by default.
- `BLASTBOX_REQUIRE_ENGINE_ALLOWLIST` is unset or false, which is the documented default.
- The attacker can submit jobs. With `BLASTBOX_API_KEY` unset, `/v1/*` and `/metrics` are open by default; with API auth configured, any authorized submitter can still create labels, and `/metrics` remains public by default unless `BLASTBOX_METRICS_PUBLIC=false`.
- The API process is long-lived enough for Prometheus client label children to accumulate.
- The attacker sends repeated small uploads with unique engine values within the global request body limit.

## Evidence Observed

Static trace evidence:

- `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:253-272` explicitly accepts any engine when the allowlist is empty and only warns unless `BLASTBOX_REQUIRE_ENGINE_ALLOWLIST` is set.
- `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:490-498` only rejects unknown engines when `_allowed_engines` is nonempty.
- `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:604` records the metric after accepted submission and store creation.
- `src/blastbox/observability/metrics.py:30-32` uses the engine value as the `engine` label.
- `src/blastbox/host/ingress/app.py:465-467` exposes all generated metrics through `/metrics`.

Bounded sink proof:

- Artifact: `/tmp/codex-security-scans/blastbox/c7e9f28495e1_20260626T144948Z/artifacts/05_findings/BB-FD-S0016-001/validation_artifacts/metrics_sink_retention_poc.py`
- Log: `/tmp/codex-security-scans/blastbox/c7e9f28495e1_20260626T144948Z/artifacts/05_findings/BB-FD-S0016-001/validation_artifacts/metrics_sink_retention_poc.log`
- The proof called the actual `record_job_submitted()` sink with four small distinct engine values.
- Observed output: child count increased from `0` to `4`; `/metrics`-style generated output increased from `4382` to `5211` bytes; there were `8` matching metric lines for the four labels; after `gc.collect()` and another scrape, retained child count remained `4` and output size remained `5211`.

Setup and proof attempts:

- `metrics_label_cardinality_poc.log`: initial run with `python` failed because `python` is not present on PATH.
- `metrics_label_cardinality_poc.python3.log`: TestClient path failed because `starlette.testclient` requires missing `httpx`.
- `metrics_label_cardinality_poc.endpoint.log` and `metrics_label_cardinality_poc.endpoint.unbuffered.log`: in-process route-endpoint attempt built the app and logged the open allowlist/auth defaults, then hung during async submission in this sandbox and was interrupted. This is treated as a proof gap for full HTTP reproduction, not as counterevidence.

## Counterevidence Considered

- A nonempty `allowed_engines` set rejects unknown engine values before spooling and before `record_job_submitted()`. This mitigates deployments that configure a finite allowlist, but the documented default is empty/all.
- `BLASTBOX_REQUIRE_ENGINE_ALLOWLIST=1` makes an empty allowlist a startup error. This is a valid operator hardening control, but it is explicitly opt-in.
- Body-size and upload-concurrency limits bound individual requests and simultaneous spooling. They do not bound cumulative distinct label children or `/metrics` response growth across accepted submissions.
- The contract `Envelope.engine` field has a `max_length=64`, but that applies to worker output envelopes, not ingress job submission or the submission metric path.
- Dispatcher unknown-engine handling fails jobs later, but the submission metric child has already been created and no cleanup path was found.

## Remaining Uncertainty

- Full HTTP multipart reproduction was not completed in this environment due missing `httpx` and an in-process async route harness hang. The static route trace is exact, and the bounded proof demonstrates the Prometheus retention behavior at the vulnerable sink.
- No high-cardinality or high-memory stress was run by design. The proof demonstrates linear child and scrape-output growth with four labels; it does not measure an outage threshold.
- Operational severity depends on whether a deployment configures `BLASTBOX_ALLOWED_ENGINES`, `BLASTBOX_REQUIRE_ENGINE_ALLOWLIST`, API auth, and private metrics.

## Minimal Next Step

Add a regression test or fix that canonicalizes/rejects submission metric labels under an open allowlist, for example recording unknown/open-allowlist engines under a bounded label such as `unknown` or requiring a finite allowlist before per-engine labels are emitted. A full HTTP regression can be added once `httpx` is available in the test environment.

## Validation Artifacts

- `/tmp/codex-security-scans/blastbox/c7e9f28495e1_20260626T144948Z/artifacts/05_findings/BB-FD-S0016-001/validation_artifacts/metrics_sink_retention_poc.py`
- `/tmp/codex-security-scans/blastbox/c7e9f28495e1_20260626T144948Z/artifacts/05_findings/BB-FD-S0016-001/validation_artifacts/metrics_sink_retention_poc.log`
- `/tmp/codex-security-scans/blastbox/c7e9f28495e1_20260626T144948Z/artifacts/05_findings/BB-FD-S0016-001/validation_artifacts/metrics_label_cardinality_poc.py`
- `/tmp/codex-security-scans/blastbox/c7e9f28495e1_20260626T144948Z/artifacts/05_findings/BB-FD-S0016-001/validation_artifacts/metrics_label_cardinality_poc.log`
- `/tmp/codex-security-scans/blastbox/c7e9f28495e1_20260626T144948Z/artifacts/05_findings/BB-FD-S0016-001/validation_artifacts/metrics_label_cardinality_poc.python3.log`
- `/tmp/codex-security-scans/blastbox/c7e9f28495e1_20260626T144948Z/artifacts/05_findings/BB-FD-S0016-001/validation_artifacts/metrics_label_cardinality_poc.endpoint.log`
- `/tmp/codex-security-scans/blastbox/c7e9f28495e1_20260626T144948Z/artifacts/05_findings/BB-FD-S0016-001/validation_artifacts/metrics_label_cardinality_poc.endpoint.unbuffered.log`

