# Security Review: blastbox

## Scope

Repository-wide security scan of the current `/home/coz/Downloads/blastbox` workspace. The scan reviewed 97 source-like files selected from the repository inventory and wrote all scan artifacts under `/tmp/codex-security-scans/blastbox/c7e9f28495e1_20260626T144948Z`.

- Scan mode: repository
- Target kind: git_worktree
- Target ID: local-blastbox-2dc4baf66184f3bc
- Revision: c7e9f28495e12ffd9e41f9c914f3da6814f3dcc9
- Snapshot digest: codex-security-snapshot/v1:sha256:4fe80fcb84e4aaa48eaaba1437c0bde95d290a92bffbfce3b9c9b70b8328b4b2
- Inventory strategy: repository
- Included paths: .
- Excluded paths: none
- Runtime or test status: No project source files were modified. Validation used static traces plus bounded local PoCs; privileged libvirt/iptables and full HTTP TestClient reproductions were not available in this environment.
- Artifacts reviewed: artifacts/01_context/threat_model.md, artifacts/02_discovery/work_ledger.jsonl, artifacts/03_coverage/repository_coverage_ledger.md, artifacts/05_findings/validation_summary.md, artifacts/05_findings/attack_path_summary.md
- Scan context: Threat model was generated during the scan from repository code, docs, and tests.

Limitations and exclusions:
